: Any physiological, mental or psychological disorder or condition, including those that are episodic or in remission, that substantially limits one or more major life activities when active', '. • Interview Process If contacted for an interview, a qualified individual with a disability should notify the University Director of Human Resources at that time if an accommodation is needed in order to participate in the interview and, if so the nature of the accommodation. The Director shall notify and collaborate with the ADA Coordinator to address the accommodation request', '. All sound must be terminated at the start of the game. Noise amplification and music must be kept to a reasonable level. Only Clean Music/Radio Version may be played at tailgate. • Soliciting or selling goods/services will not be permitted on stadium grounds without prior approval from the university. • Except as may be specifically authorized by University Police, the operation of drones/unmanned aircraft systems on University property is prohibited', '. Publicly available applications driven by AI, including generative AI that includes large language models (LLMs), chatbots, or image generators, are widely popular. This policy highlights the unique issues raised by AI, helps employees understand the guidelines for its acceptable use, and protects the university’s confidential information, intellectual property, culture, commitment to diversity, and brand', '. • Benefits and Privileges of Employment An employee seeking an accommodation related to the benefits and/or privileges associated with employment should notify the immediate supervisor. The immediate superior shall notify and collaborate with the ADA Coordinator to address the accommodation request. Such request should include the benefits and/or privilege of employment in which the individual is unable to participate and the accommodation requested']], 'uris': None, 'included': ['metadatas', 'documents', 'distances'], 'data': None, 'meta